  <data name="Tip.InputFormat" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sample format used to open the recording device.&#10;Auto: uses the first one that opens, in the order Float32 → Int32 → Int24 → Int16.&#10;If you pick one: an error occurs when the device cannot be opened in that format.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.Cushion" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Extra headroom added to the ring buffer between input and output.&#10;Larger values make dropouts less likely, and add the same amount of latency.&#10;Default: no extra.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.OutputFormat" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Sample format used to open the playback device.&#10;Integer formats (Int16/Int24): values are rounded and dither is added when converting.&#10;Auto: uses the first one that opens, in the order Float32 → Int32 → Int24 → Int16.&#10;If you pick one: an error occurs when the device cannot be opened in that format.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.Dither" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Noise added before rounding to integer output (Int24/Int16 for playback and for recording).&#10;TPDF: Standard. Turns the rounding error into white noise that does not depend on the signal.&#10;          Recommended if you will edit or master the audio later.&#10;HP-TPDF: Same distribution, with the noise shifted toward high frequencies.&#10;Noise shaping: Reduces noise in the easily audible midrange and moves it to high frequencies (total noise increases).&#10;Off: Rounding only.&#10;Has no effect for Float32 and Int32.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.RecordFolder" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Where recording files are saved.&#10;You can paste a path. A folder that does not exist is created when recording starts.&#10;Default: Music\Koromogae</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.RecordDepth" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bit depth of the recording file (WAV / FLAC).&#10;Int24 / Int16: rounded, with dither added according to the dither mode.&#10;Float32: no rounding and no dither (the file gets larger). Available for WAV only.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.RecordFormat" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>File format of the recording.&#10;WAV: uncompressed. Can be saved as Float32 / Int24 / Int16.&#10;FLAC: lossless compression (the sound is exactly the same, about half the size). Int24 / Int16 only; Float32 cannot be saved.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.RecordOptions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Choose the FLAC compression level (0-8).&#10;Not available for WAV. Cannot be changed while recording.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.RecordDry" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Also records the unprocessed sound (before the plugins) to a separate file (..._dry.wav / ..._dry.flac).&#10;The processed sound is delayed by the plugin latency (it is not compensated).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.RecordButton" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Records the processed sound to a file.&#10;Available only while running (after pressing Start).&#10;Stopping also ends the recording.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.Latency" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>An estimate of the end-to-end latency.&#10;Input / Output: values reported by PortAudio&#10;Internal buffer: measured average of the buffer between input and output&#10;Plugins: total latency reported by the enabled plugins&#10;Latency inside the device itself (for example USB devices) is not included.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Tip.Diagnostics" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Numbers for investigating the cause of dropouts.&#10;Dropouts: how many times the buffer ran empty during playback and the sound went silent (cumulative since start)&#10;Discarded: share of audio discarded in bulk (oldest first) because too much had accumulated (cumulative since start)&#10;Headroom: the headroom secured by the engine (the duration of audio in the most recent input callback)&#10;Device XRUN: number of input/output device overflows/underflows reported by PortAudio (cumulative since start)&#10;The following are shown only when they happen (red):&#10;Callback exceptions: number of exceptions in audio processing (cumulative since start; details in app.log)&#10;Callback has stopped: input/output has not run for 1.5 s or more (disappears when it resumes)&#10;Recording lost: the length filled with silence because writing could not keep up</value>
  </data>
